{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788193132,"nonce":"jbNwElcqgn1oejthdFVu8M4pbTU=","title":"things emits an addressable list ordered by a live score — same bug as pawns, same fix","message":"Found by the worker on `1eb2262` while fixing the same shape in `pawns`. Flagged\nand deliberately not filed without Evan's call; he called it 2026-08-31.\n\n`Source/AutoRimmer/ThingVerbs.cs` emits a `things` list whose entries carry\n`thingIDNumber` — i.e. an ADDRESSABLE list, one a caller can and will hold\nhandles into — ordered `attention-desc` on a score computed live at read time.\n\nThat is exactly the defect fixed in `pawns`: **an index into a list ordered by a\nmoving value is not a handle.** Two reads seconds apart can return the same\nentries in a different order with nothing in the world having been added or\nremoved, because the score itself moved. In `pawns` this cost spec 3.4 six\nacceptance checks and produced a wrong diagnosis from me before a worker traced\nthe real cause.\n\nTHE FIX IS ALREADY DESIGNED — apply the pattern, do not reinvent it.\n`spec/stable-pawn-order` separates SELECTION from PRESENTATION:\n\n- Attention-desc still decides WHICH entries survive the cap. That is spec 2.6's\n  rule — a cap must never hide the urgent item — and it must be preserved.\n- The re-sort to `thingIDNumber` ascending runs on the SURVIVORS only, never on\n  the candidate set.\n- The result publishes both facts (`order`, `selected_by`), and every line\n  carries `attention_rank` so urgency survives the reorder instead of being\n  destroyed by it.\n- An `order` argument lets a caller ask for the attention view explicitly.\n\nRead that branch first; this should end up a near-mechanical port, and any\ndivergence from it wants a reason.\n\nThe general rule is landing in DESIGN.md via that same branch: an observer's\nlist has two orders, and publishing only one makes it unholdable. This issue is\nthe second instance, which is the argument for the rule being general rather\nthan a one-off.\n\nAcceptance\n- `things` emits by `thingIDNumber` ascending by default, selects by attention,\n  and publishes both facts plus per-entry `attention_rank`.\n- The cap still keeps the highest-attention entries — demonstrate with a capped\n  read that the urgent item is present.\n- Two reads with a score change in between (and no add/remove) return the same\n  entries in the same order.\n- Consistent with `pawns`: same argument name, same field names, same vocabulary.","files":null}]}